<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0
  Copyright the Karst contributors.

  Karst.app's own entitlements — ADR-0026 item 7. A host app must hold
  `com.apple.developer.system-extension.install` before
  `OSSystemExtensionRequest.activationRequest` (SystemExtensionActivator.swift)
  can do anything at all: without it, `submitRequest` fails immediately with
  no user-approval prompt ever shown, which is a different, earlier failure
  than ADR-0026 item 1's still-pending entitlement application (that one
  gates whether the *extension's* own NetworkExtension entitlement is
  trusted, not whether the host app may ask to install it).

  `com.apple.developer.networking.networkextension` added after a real,
  documented failure (#159): `NETunnelProviderManager.saveToPreferences`
  failed on real hardware with `NEVPNErrorDomain Code=5 "permission
  denied"` / `nehelper`'s "Failed to obtain authorization right... no
  authorization provided" — even though the host app's provisioning
  profile granted "Personal VPN" (`com.apple.developer.networking.vpn.api`).
  Per Apple DTS (developer.apple.com/forums/thread/807080): "Personal VPN"
  is for the built-in IKEv2/IPsec transports, not for
  `NEPacketTunnelProvider`'s custom-transport VPN, which Karst uses — mixing
  the two causes exactly this conflict. The fix is the *same*
  `networkextension` entitlement the extension itself carries
  (`PacketTunnel.entitlements`), on **both** the host app and the extension,
  not Personal VPN on the host app at all. `karststatus.provisionprofile`
  needs regenerating to match (Network Extension capability on
  `dev.karst.karststatus`'s App ID, Personal VPN removed) — this file alone
  is not sufficient without that.

  Scoped to these two entitlements rather than merged into a broader
  "Karst.app capabilities" file: KarstStatus does not otherwise touch any
  hardened-runtime-gated capability, and adding entitlements nothing in the
  app uses is exactly the kind of unreviewed scope creep a signed bundle
  should not carry silently.
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.developer.system-extension.install</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.developer.networking.networkextension</key>
    <array>
        <string>packet-tunnel-provider-systemextension</string>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
